============================== Start [case_nan_propagation,(),{}]
    input row 1 contains NaN at column 2: [5.0, 6.0, nan, 8.0]
    reduce sum  per row = [10.0, nan, 42.0]   numpy: [10.0, nan, 42.0]   -> same as numpy
    reduce max  per row = [4.0, 8.0, 12.0]   numpy: [4.0, nan, 12.0]   -> DIFFERS from numpy
    reduce min  per row = [1.0, 5.0, 9.0]   numpy: [1.0, nan, 9.0]   -> DIFFERS from numpy
    SUM propagates the NaN; MAX and MIN drop it. A NaN that is obvious in a sum is
    invisible to a max-reduction, so max is not a NaN detector.
============================== End   [case_nan_propagation]
